                     <title ref="LIT0049IHA#s18IHA"/>
                     <incipit xml:lang="ar">
                        <locus target="#1v">-1v</locus>رَجَعْتُمْ إِلَيْهِمْ ۚ قُل كر اذا تَعْتَذِرُوا لَن نُّؤْمِنَ<note>9:94</note>
                     </incipit>
                     <explicit xml:lang="ar">
                        <locus target="#45r">-45r</locus>وَمَا يُعْلِنُونَ إِنَّهُ عَلِيمٌ بِذَاتِ الصُّدُورِ <note>11:5</note>
                     </explicit>
                     <note>9:94-11:5. Some words are divided into two different lines.
The “ḏāl” is written with the dot inside. Sometimes the catchword is only the first part of the first word in the next page, sometimes there is a repeated word and the catchword is the second word of the next page. 
The name of the scribe appears in mss. 4521D (37r) and 4521X (1v, 45v). The note stating that he is actually the scribe is in 4521X (45v).   In 15r-v and 20r-v there is a different kind of paper but the text goes on normally
</note>
